WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:03.540
- My freshman year of
college, I cheated on a final,

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:05.690
and this is that story.

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:09.790
Okay, before we start, cheating
might be a strong word.

00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:11.760
Actually, maybe it's not.

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:13.543
I'll leave that up to all of you.

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:16.440
Okay, here we go.

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:18.890
So I was home on a
little break from school.

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:22.030
Nothing holiday related, just
a weekend at my parents house.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:24.050
It was Sunday and I was leaving that night

00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:25.340
to fly back to school.

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:28.900
My point being school and home
were not close to each other.

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:30.780
If I'm being honest, it's a little tough

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:32.750
to go to school in a place
that's far from home.

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:34.250
Especially if you're someone like me

00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:36.100
who gets homesick from time to time.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:38.780
Anyways, it was end of
April, Spring semester

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:42.150
was winding down a.k.a finals season.

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:43.940
The pressure was on.

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:44.924
I'm gonna be bold here,

00:00:44.924 --> 00:00:48.830
I'd classify myself as
in intelligent person.

00:00:48.830 --> 00:00:51.808
Now when I say that, would
I call myself a genius?

00:00:51.808 --> 00:00:53.170
I don't think I would.

00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:54.703
Would I call myself dumb?

00:00:54.703 --> 00:00:56.160
I don't think I would.

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:59.510
And I like school, I like learning

00:00:59.510 --> 00:01:02.900
so I'm not really sure what came over me

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:05.490
on that faithful day.

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:07.240
Before I knew it, I was heading back

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:08.770
to school on that Sunday night.

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:12.440
I had a final the very next
morning, Monday morning.

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:15.967
For whatever reason, before
I even left my parents house,

00:01:15.967 --> 00:01:20.690
I thought to myself, I'm not
taking that test tomorrow.

00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:22.550
I'm gonna email my teacher now,

00:01:22.550 --> 00:01:24.424
tell him my flight got canceled

00:01:24.424 --> 00:01:26.580
and I could take it later that week.

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:30.050
My thought was, I could buy
myself a couple extra days

00:01:30.050 --> 00:01:32.610
and get ready for the test in my own time.

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:34.250
It was a slam dunk.

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:36.520
I guarantee a surefire plan.

00:01:37.791 --> 00:01:40.230
Maybe I was a genius.

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:44.740
I sent the email, got on to
my very not canceled flight,

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:45.850
and went back to school.

00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:48.231
I'm feeling good, real slick.

00:01:48.231 --> 00:01:51.030
Until I get back to my dorm.

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:54.277
There's a reply to my email.

00:01:54.277 --> 00:01:55.740
"Hi Brigid."

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:57.147
Perfectly acceptable greeting.

00:01:57.147 --> 00:01:59.917
"No problem, sorry to
hear about your flight.

00:01:59.917 --> 00:02:01.787
"Just bring me proof of your new flight,

00:02:01.787 --> 00:02:03.487
"and we'll be all good."

00:02:03.487 --> 00:02:06.200
(clock ticking)

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:07.460
How did this happen?

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:10.650
This was supposed to be an easy plan.

00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:13.310
Okay, okay, okay, just calm down.

00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:16.576
I have no choice but to
own up to my mistakes

00:02:16.576 --> 00:02:20.260
and face the situation that I've created.

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:21.860
Or...

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:24.940
Or, and hear me out, I look up

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:29.040
I don't know, a template
for a plane ticket,

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:32.630
create a fake boarding pass
to present to my professor.

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:34.320
I was in too deep.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:35.650
I couldn't confess.

00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:39.570
This became Operation Fake Ticket.

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:42.270
We arrange a new time
for me to take the final,

00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:43.590
that's a few days away.

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:46.630
I needed to craft something
that was believable.

00:02:46.630 --> 00:02:50.220
Actually, more than believable, authentic.

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:53.620
He's a smart guy, he's
a college professor.

00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:56.190
He could probably look
up if a flight was real.

00:02:56.190 --> 00:03:01.190
So I just needed to make it
seem like I was on that flight.

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:05.420
I was starting to feel like
I was a character on Lost.

00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:10.420
Somehow, after days of
studying, and terrifying nights

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:15.980
of dreams of expulsion,
I completed both tasks.

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:18.913
Not only was I ready for my final,

00:03:20.176 --> 00:03:22.520
I was ready for the greatest
trick I'd ever pull.

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:24.200
It was the day of the test.

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:26.510
I walk into his classroom,

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:29.590
my heart is pounding out of my chest.

00:03:29.590 --> 00:03:31.017
There he is.

00:03:31.017 --> 00:03:34.160
I'm trying to figure
out what he's thinking.

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:37.460
So far, he seems oddly calm.

00:03:37.460 --> 00:03:38.910
I think I'm ready for this test,

00:03:38.910 --> 00:03:42.060
and oh here's that airline
information you asked for.

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:45.550
I hand over the goods, he
looks them over briefly

00:03:45.550 --> 00:03:47.240
and sets them down.

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:52.240
Internally I'm like, and
that's how it's done baby,

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:54.617
we just pulled this off.

00:03:54.617 --> 00:03:56.057
"Okay, cool!

00:03:56.057 --> 00:03:57.567
"So while you take the test,"

00:03:57.567 --> 00:03:59.147
"I'll just give the airline a call

00:03:59.147 --> 00:04:01.047
"to make sure you were on the flight."

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:03.093
Excuse me?

00:04:03.093 --> 00:04:05.331
I'm surprised I didn't
just burst into flames

00:04:05.331 --> 00:04:06.920
right then and there.

00:04:06.920 --> 00:04:09.557
Yeah, no, of course, that sounds good.

00:04:09.557 --> 00:04:11.660
I'm trying to play it cool.

00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:14.420
He hands over the test, I take a seat

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:17.753
at the desk in his classroom,
my life, it was over.

00:04:17.753 --> 00:04:18.995
This is it.

00:04:18.995 --> 00:04:20.770
This is how it ends.

00:04:20.770 --> 00:04:25.190
He leaves the room, I take the test.

00:04:25.190 --> 00:04:28.000
Oddly enough, he never returns.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.445
I leave my finished test on his desk,

00:04:30.445 --> 00:04:35.030
leave the classroom and never looked back.

00:04:35.030 --> 00:04:38.520
Do you have any idea how hard it is

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:41.070
to focus on a test when your teacher

00:04:41.070 --> 00:04:42.810
is trying to catch you in a lie?

00:04:42.810 --> 00:04:45.480
I could feel my brain melting.

00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:48.101
I sprung back to my dorm,
collect all my friends,

00:04:48.101 --> 00:04:50.517
explain the new development in the saga.

00:04:50.517 --> 00:04:52.597
"I feel like you can't
just call an airline

00:04:52.597 --> 00:04:54.120
"and get that information."

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:55.720
Says one of smart friends.

00:04:55.720 --> 00:04:57.740
Yeah, yeah that makes sense.

00:04:57.740 --> 00:04:59.641
For whatever reason, I had my friend call

00:04:59.641 --> 00:05:02.420
instead of me and ask the airline

00:05:02.420 --> 00:05:04.670
if my name came up in a flight manifest.

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:07.640
They wouldn't give the information out.

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:08.473
Delightful.

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:10.850
Nice try buddy.

00:05:10.850 --> 00:05:14.460
I did it, there's no
way he could call me out

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:16.440
on my fake plane ticket now.

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:17.400
And guess what?

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:21.180
A week or so later, I found
out I got an A on that test.

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:22.960
This wasn't all for nothing.

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:25.577
Heads up, the craziest part of this story

00:05:25.577 --> 00:05:27.390
hasn't even happened yet.

00:05:27.390 --> 00:05:30.580
Freshman year ends, I end up
transferring to another school,

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:33.280
it was closer to home and
just a little more my speed.

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:37.137
One day, I'm sitting on campus
waiting for a class to start

00:05:37.137 --> 00:05:40.920
and suddenly, there's
an odd shift in the air.

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:42.610
You know when you can just feel

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:44.227
when something is about to happen?

00:05:44.227 --> 00:05:45.620
"Brigid, right?"

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:46.860
I hear a voice ask.

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:49.610
I look up, my heart stops.

00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:51.305
It's my fucking teacher.

00:05:51.305 --> 00:05:53.340
The guy that I duped.

00:05:53.340 --> 00:05:54.780
He's staring at me.

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:57.920
Yes, it's me, Brigid.

00:05:57.920 --> 00:05:58.753
How are you?

00:05:58.753 --> 00:06:00.810
"Good to see you." He says.

00:06:00.810 --> 00:06:04.188
Starts to walk away, I swear on my life,

00:06:04.188 --> 00:06:06.387
I'm not making this up.

00:06:06.387 --> 00:06:08.427
"Nice job with that plane ticket."

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:10.680
What is this?

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:12.150
A goddamn movie?

00:06:12.150 --> 00:06:13.760
People don't talk like that,

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:15.800
this doesn't happen in real life.

00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:17.500
Apparently this happens in my life.

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:19.330
What was he even doing here?

00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:21.470
Why was he at my new school?

00:06:21.470 --> 00:06:24.540
I have expected him to do
that thing in scary movies

00:06:24.540 --> 00:06:29.090
where he crosses a street, a
bus drives by and disappears.

00:06:29.090 --> 00:06:32.040
Obviously, I go home and
look him up immediately.

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:35.240
Turns out, he's an adjunct
professor at my new school.

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:38.670
Oddly enough, we never crossed
paths again after that.

00:06:38.670 --> 00:06:40.145
I think he just wanted to see

00:06:40.145 --> 00:06:43.050
how far I would take my lie.

00:06:43.050 --> 00:06:45.040
And he got his answer.

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:47.660
I took that lie all the way.

00:06:47.660 --> 00:06:49.460
Did I learn my lesson?

00:06:49.460 --> 00:06:50.540
Yep.

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:52.390
Would I do it again?

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:53.650
Nope.

00:06:53.650 --> 00:06:55.328
Stay in school kids.

00:06:55.328 --> 00:06:58.328
(upbeat jazz music)

